    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοῖ </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοἵ</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			A.D.
			<u>Synt.</u>
			320.1
		</span></i>, cf. Lat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>euhoe</i>),
			exclamation used in the cult of Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1294
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαί,
			εὐάν</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοῖ σαβοῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.260
				</span></i>
			: as an interjection, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναταράσσει—εὐοῖ—μ᾽
					ὁ κισσός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					219
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
